'''Season fifteen''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'', called '''''Dancing with the Stars: All-Stars''''',<ref name=abc/> premiered on September 24, 2012, on the [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] network.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2012/07/26/abc-announces-premiere-dates-for-modern-family-the-middle-dwts-greys-anatomy-once-upon-a-time-more/142961/ |title=ABC Announces Fall Premiere Dates: 'Modern Family', 'Revenge', 'DWTS:All-Stars', 'Grey's Anatomy', 'Once Upon a Time' & More - Ratings |publisher=Zap2it |access-date=2012-08-15 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120828201742/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2012/07/26/abc-announces-premiere-dates-for-modern-family-the-middle-dwts-greys-anatomy-once-upon-a-time-more/142961/ |archive-date=2012-08-28 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Season 15 was the first to feature an "all-star" cast of returning celebrities.<ref name=abc>{{cite web |url=http://beta.abc.go.com/shows/dancing-with-the-stars/cast-the-all-star-season/0-cast-season-15-of-dwts |title=Dancing With The Stars - ABC.com |publisher=Beta.abc.go.com |access-date=2012-08-15 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120821163034/http://beta.abc.go.com/shows/dancing-with-the-stars/cast-the-all-star-season/0-cast-season-15-of-dwts |archive-date=2012-08-21 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Six of the returning finalists had already won the title in prior seasons: [[Kelly Monaco]], [[Drew Lachey]], [[Emmitt Smith]], [[Apolo Anton Ohno]], [[Hélio Castroneves]], and [[Shawn Johnson East|Shawn Johnson]]. Additionally, it was the only season to date to offer fractional (0.5) scores. Five contestants reunited with their original partners ([[Emmitt Smith]], [[Joey Fatone]], [[Melissa Rycroft]], [[Bristol Palin]], [[Kirstie Alley]]), while the other eight danced with new partners.

[[Dancing with the Stars (American season 8)|Season 8]] finalist [[Melissa Rycroft]] defeated season 8 champion Shawn Johnson and [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 1)|season 1]] champion Kelly Monaco to win the trophy. This also marked the first win for professional [[Tony Dovolani]].

==Cast==

===Couples===
This season featured thirteen returning celebrity contestants. The first twelve celebrities were revealed on July 27, 2012.<ref>{{cite web|author= |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/ustv/s92/dancingwiththestars/news/a395839/dancing-with-the-stars-all-stars-bristol-palin-kirstie-alley-more.html|title=Dancing with the Stars: All-Stars: Bristol Palin, Kirstie Alley, more - Dancing with the Stars News - Reality TV|publisher=Digital Spy|date=2012-07-27|access-date=2012-08-15|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120728235817/http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/ustv/s92/dancingwiththestars/news/a395839/dancing-with-the-stars-all-stars-bristol-palin-kirstie-alley-more.html|archive-date=2012-07-28|url-status=live}}</ref> A thirteenth contestant was chosen by the public, from either [[Sabrina Bryan]], [[Kyle Massey]], or [[Carson Kressley]]. Sabrina Bryan was announced the winner on August 27.<ref>{{cite web|author=Lanford Beard |url=http://insidetv.ew.com/2012/08/27/dancing-with-the-stars-sabrina-bryan-viewers-choice/|title='Dancing With the Stars': Sabrina Bryan wins viewers' choice vote |publisher=Entertainment Weekly|date=2012-08-27|access-date=2012-08-27|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120828160610/http://insidetv.ew.com/2012/08/27/dancing-with-the-stars-sabrina-bryan-viewers-choice/|archive-date=2012-08-28|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Louis van Amstel]] was partnered with Bryan, while the professional partners for the first twelve celebrities were revealed on August 13.<ref>{{cite web|author= |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/ustv/s92/dancingwiththestars/news/a399081/dancing-with-the-stars-all-stars-professional-partners-confirmed.html|title='Dancing with the Stars All-Stars': Professional partners confirmed - Dancing with the Stars News - Reality TV|publisher=Digital Spy|date=2012-08-13|access-date=2012-08-15|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120825050901/http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/ustv/s92/dancingwiththestars/news/a399081/dancing-with-the-stars-all-stars-professional-partners-confirmed.html|archive-date=2012-08-25|url-status=live}}</ref> The members of the dance troupe for this season were [[Oksana Dmytrenko]], [[Emma Slater]], [[Sharna Burgess]], [[Henry Byalikov]], [[Sasha Farber]], and [[Sonny Fredie-Pedersen]].

